    • My chosen design and materials.
    • The door and mechanism is all mounted on the inside of the coop.
    • Door sliders are made of wood, the door is a sloppy fit to ensure no binding.
    • 3D printed adjustable slider points (2 on each side) take up the sloppy fit of the door with no binding.
    • The door is made from a piece of Aluminium checker plate 3mm thick.
    • The motor is a gearbox motor JGB37-520, 22RPM. . Do check for grease in the gearbox as mine was as good as dry
    • 3D printed motor mount
    • 31mm aluminium v groove pulley, giving the perfect speed ratio of opening and closing the door.
    • The door suspension can be easily be made from 70-80lb monofilament fishing line.(thin,flexible and reliable)
    • A metal clip for easy disconnecting the door.
    • The black cylindrical object attached to the line is a lead weight weighing around 150 g.
      It keeps the line taut if the door encounters an obstruction (such as a chicken), 
      allowing the door obstruction detection to operate correctly.
    • 2 X 5mm red LEDs above the door start to flash at sunset to call the chickens home, when the door closes the
      flashing pattern changes for visual varication the door has secured close.(they flash until sunrise)
